# @hub-lanes

# ── ARCHIE WHOLE-FACTORY WATCH LANE (BH-4586) ───────────────────────────────
# Cron fires every 10 minutes (offset to :07, off the queue doctor's minute);
# a tick acts once per archie.watch.interval_min (D1 settings, default 20, so
# :07, :27 and :47) and the other ticks exit at once. A tick that acts reads
# the open alerts plus four sweeps (unrescued reviews, hub inodes, merged lanes
# missing from crontab, paused projects with work waiting) and pulls ONE lever
# per incident from a fixed allowlist: ack and route the alert, kick the owning
# lane, run disk-clean on the hub, re-run the failed deploy, or file a ticket.
# An incident still open after archie.watch.escalate_s gets ONE ticket. Every
# action is an archie_actions row claimed before any write; flock -n dedupes.
# Off: ARCHIE_FMW_ENABLED=0, flags/lane-off-archie-fm-watch,
# bin/harness-ctl.sh off archie-fm-watch, or the settings row archie.manage=off.
7-57/10 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/archie-fm-watch.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
